      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1884 the Oregon‑California Railroad turned Grants Pass into a railhead, drawing miners, farmers, and lumbermen.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grantspassoregon.gov/395/History",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Rogue Theatre downtown now hosts local performing arts, preserving a long‑standing cultural venue.",
